00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
bill gates is likely the most well-known  billionaire in the entire world everyone  knows him as the child prodigy that  dropped out of harvard and founded one  of the biggest companies in the world  microsoft since then he's dominated the  top of the billionaires list currently  standing at 112 billion dollars and  that's after donating more than 50  billion dollars to charity clearly  finding microsoft has worked out  extremely well for bill  but bill wasn't the sole founder of  microsoft in fact microsoft was actually  co-founded by another child prodigy  named paul allen and this wasn't just  some honorary title either like apple's  co-founder ronald wayne paul was heavily  involved in the company for nearly a  decade before he decided to part ways at  the time he owned roughly 25 of  microsoft which at the peak would  translate to 625 billion dollars yet  most people have no idea that microsoft  even had a co-founder or that he  tragically died just a few years ago so  here's what happened to the forgotten  founder of microsoft  taking a look back paul allen was born  on january 21 1953 in seattle washington  he was born to a pretty academic family  as both of his parents were heavily  involved in libraries in fact his father  worked as the associate director of  libraries at the university of  washington meanwhile his mom was a  librarian hearing this i don't think  you'd be surprised to hear that his  parents put him in the best school they  could afford a private preparatory  school called lakeside for perspective  annual tuition at the school currently  cost 38 000  aside from enrolling paula in a  prestigious private school his parents  would also consistently take him to  museums galleries and concerts to expose  him to as many interests as possible but  ironically his greatest interest wasn't  any of these his greatest interest was  messing with computers with his friends  from school bill gates and kent evans  this trio would regularly use lakeside's  teletype terminals to develop their  programming skills and soon enough they  would actually found a programming club  the only problem though was that they  didn't have any access to computers so  they made a deal with the local computer  company called the computer center  corporation they offered to find bugs in  their software in exchange for computer  time and it didn't take long for them to  go from this to developing scheduling  software for lakeside  despite spending all this time on  hobbies paul never slipped up  academically either  in fact he got a perfect 1600 on the sat  before being admitted into washington  state university paul was actually two  years older than bill so bill was still  in seattle when paul went off to college  but since paul went to an state college  this made it easy for them to stay in  close contact and work on their first  year's business called trafford data at  the time state and local governments  would often perform traffic surveys in  order to make stoplights more efficient  to accomplish this they would layout  rubber hoses on the road and every time  a car passed by it would create air  pulses within the rubber hose which was  recorded by a mechanical counter paul  and bill's vision with the travel data  was to digitalize this entire process  but they once again had a fundamental  issue they didn't have access to a  computer so they partnered with a man  named paul weiner who could build them a  computer  but just as everything was starting to  get off the ground the trio would be  stopped cold in their tracks the state  of washington would develop their own  traffic processing program which they  gave out for free to local governments  so this unfortunately completely  eliminated the need for travel data by  this point paul had finished two years  of college but when he was offered a job  as a programmer at honeywell in boston  he dropped out and took the job  this was actually perfect timing because  bill would go to harvard at the same  time which is also in boston so the duo  was able to continue their friendship in  boston and it didn't take long for them  to start their next business venture  in 1975 paul and bill would begin  microsoft but the company was nothing  like what we know them as today the  company was actually focused on selling  a programming language interpreter in  new mexico one of their first client  slash partners was an up-and-coming  company called micro instrumentation and  telemetry systems and given that this  company was located in albuquerque new  mexico paul and the bill decided to base  microsoft there as well  it wasn't until four years later that  they would move the headquarters to  their home state of washington in the  meantime microsoft would get some  international exposure as well  in august of 1977 they would form an  agreement with ascii magazine in japan  which allowed them to open ascii  microsoft despite all this progress with  the company it didn't take long for bill  and paul to start developing some  animosity towards each other it all  started with a bill wanting more equity  than palm the argument from bill was  that he was still in college and making  no money but paul already had a  well-paying job  so bill was not only taking a big risk  with microsoft but he would likely be  able to spend more time on microsoft  this argument made sense to paula so he  agreed on splitting the equity 6040 but  it wasn't long before bill wanted even  more equity bill soon renegotiated a  contract to be a 64 36 split paul didn't  want to make a big deal about this and  he knew that both of them would be super  rich anyway if things worked out so he  didn't really fight back against bill  but over time things just got even worse  as microsoft started to attract press  attention bill became the public face of  microsoft which slowly ate away at  paul's significance within the company  the two were quickly growing apart and  they both knew it but paul says that he  was too angry and proud to confront bill  about it though's personality did not  make the situation any better either  according to paula bill was usually an  extremely sore loser and he often had  difficulty admitting his shortfalls for  example paul stopped playing chess with  bill very early on because bill would  often sweep the pieces onto the floor in  anger whenever he lost while such quirks  were likely quite annoying none of these  were enough for paul to leave the  company he was still extremely  optimistic about the future of microsoft  but all of this would change when he  found out that he couldn't be nearly as  optimistic about his own life in 1982 at  age 29 paul would be diagnosed with  hodgkin's lymphoma which is a type of  cancer that affects the immune system  despite this scary diagnosis paul would  stick around at microsoft but his input  into the company was significantly less  for obvious reasons however bill had a  different take on the situation instead  of supporting his friend through this  difficult period bill would start  complaining about how paul was becoming  unproductive and the breaking point was  when paul overheard bill and steve  ballmer discussing how they could reduce  paul's equity after hearing this paul  would do the honourable thing and resign  from microsoft in february of 1983.  fortunately paul's cancer would get  significantly better following his  departure from microsoft but his mental  health was worse than ever before you  see paul didn't really want to leave  microsoft he wanted to be part of  something big and he had already founded  something big but because of bill he was  unable to continue that journey it  should be noted that paul was still on  microsoft's board but this wasn't what  he wanted it per se  so he kind of just wallowed in his own  despair for a few years after leaving  microsoft but all of this would change  when microsoft went public in 1986. at  the end of their first trading day  microsoft would be valued at 780 million  dollars which gave paul a net worth of  195 million dollars paul now had both  loads of money and a life-threatening  disease that could return at any time so  i don't think you'd be surprised here  that paul decided to stop feeling sorry  for himself and started living it up  while he still could but before he did  that he wanted to start off with a  positive task  so in 1986 he founded the paul g allen  family foundation which was dedicated to  advancing health and human services  after this however paul started  splurging he of course bought all of the  classic things like mansions yachts  private jets and sports teams but he  also had several creative indulgences as  well for example paul was a massive fan  of music and especially rock music so in  2000 he opened the experience music  project which was a rock and roll museum  that was dedicated to his rock hero jimi  hendrix he also created his own band  called the underthinkers where he sang  it and played a guitar in 2013 he  launched a full album in which he  personally wrote or co-wrote every song  in the album aside from music paul also  began collecting really unique items for  example he built up a collection of  world war ii fighter planes he also had  an extensive art collection that was  filled with pieces that were worth tens  of millions each paul didn't just spend  all of his money though he also invested  significant portions of it for example  he had stakes in america online and  dreamworks his sports bets also ended up  playing up pretty well as he owned the  seattle seahawks the portland  trailblazers and the seattle sounders  the seahawks would end up making it to  the super bowl three times and they even  won in 2014  not all of his investments went so  smoothly though paul definitely had his  fair share of losses which in his case  were massive one of his investments  charter communications held for  bankruptcy while many of his other pet  projects including asymmetrics star wave  metrocom and interval research never  lived up to what he envisioned  nonetheless his stake in microsoft and  his other successful investments were  more than enough to make up for these  given that he would end up with a net  worth of 20 billion dollars  in terms of paul's relationship with  bill gates after the fallout they did  eventually make amends and get back onto  a talking basis but it was never quite  the same paul stuck around on microsoft  sport up until 2000 at which point he  left as bill gates stepped down from  being ceo  unfortunately paul's lymphoma would  resurface in 2009 and it though he would  get treatment he was no doubt getting  weaker and weaker as paul saw the end of  his life approaching he decided to write  a memoir called idea man that told the  story of microsoft from his perspective  in the book he claims that it was  actually him who came up with a bunch of  the ideas that bill gates often gets  credit for for example paul says that he  was the one who came up with the name  microsoft and that he created a soft  card and that he was the one who thought  of targeting the personal computer  market according to paula he was the one  that came up with all of the ideas while  bill spent most of his time running the  business itself many critics have  pointed out that the book is filled with  bitterness and that it's more of a rant  than an inspiring memoir but none of  that really matters though as paul's  lymphoma would return yet again in 2018  and it would take his life on october 15  2018 at age 65. in terms of what will  happen to his 4th gen paul never got  married and had no children so he  doesn't have any errors that will take  over paul's goal was to simply donate  all of his money after his death and he  wrote a detailed plan regarding how to  do that so all that's left is for his  sister jody allen to actually execute  his final vision he was never able to be  the leading voice at microsoft but  hopefully he will be the leading voice  regarding the future of his fortune  would you guys rather be rich and sick  or poor and healthy comment that down  below  also drop a like if you agree that paul  allen is underrated and of course  consider checking out our discord  community to suggest future video ideas  and consider subscribing and see more  questions logically answered but until  then i'm hari and i'll see you guys on  the next one  you

